{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1472236-stats-for-ubiquitous-nova-tech-in-aeon","id":1472236,"title":"Stats for Ubiquitous Nova Tech in Aeon","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: \u00c6on"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-01-11T05:01:58-08:00","id":1472236,"title":"Stats for Ubiquitous Nova Tech in Aeon","content":"Specifically, what would the stats be for gravity crystals? They're buildable by normal people, I assume, using black box plans that are provided by the Nova that initially creates the tech. Unless they actually do need a Nova to build them and in Aeon Psion's are able to sub in for Nova's in the creation process? Would gravity crystals be buildable by a player character? Like if a player wanted to be the in-universe origin of gravity crystals could they do it with the rules as written? Would you use some kind of scaled down gravity manipulation, or a gravity ray that was reduced in intensity and increase in width? Considering the tech would mostly be used for fluff purposes (the long term effects of micro gravity on bones probably not going to be relevant in a game) would it just be best to have the GM assign the number of dots it would take to build something like an artificial gravity device?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27133-planguy","name":"Planguy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-11T08:44:35-08:00","id":1472243,"title":"","content":"I think that we should assume that those are coretech (Nova creates technology that has been integrated into common knowledge).<br /> <br /> So, they are just trinkets, like an airplane.<br /> <br /> If you wand to do something fancy you could build inspired supertech based on those elements.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25829-vjornin","name":"Vjornin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-11T09:07:40-08:00","id":1472244,"title":"","content":"GravCrystals are just a very specific effect of Elemental Mastery (Gravity) that was made Core tech.<br /> <br /> in thesis you dont need a nova to invent grav crystals, humans needed a nova to invent it faster, but the Coalision ark have an artificial gravity system that works similarly to gravcrystals, but was not invented by novas.<br /> <br /> The point is, Q-Tech is completely supernatural, Inspired tech is impossible following the real world physics laws, but with that extra (like a Nova blood drop or psi energy) it becomes possible, and Advanced Tech is completely possible to reach by anyone, but may take a LONG time and a lot of tech studies to reach.<br /> <br /> How does it work? I have no idea, maybe there is a material that can generate gravitional fields, or maybe it is not really gravity but a eletromagnetic field with a very precise configuration, but gravcrystals are possibel following the TC regular physics laws, like Warp Speed is possible in Startrek universe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-11T11:39:17-08:00","id":1472250,"title":"","content":"And to be clear, Aberrant has rules for how to turn Q-Tech into core-tech, making it into something that can be manufactured and used by anyone with the right facilities instead of needing the involvement of Novas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-11T14:36:59-08:00","id":1472266,"title":"","content":"Is turning stuff into coretech in the main Aberrant book?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27133-planguy","name":"Planguy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-11T14:44:08-08:00","id":1472267,"title":"","content":"Yes. It's under reverse engineering.<br /> <br /> The Nova starts by taking his q-tech invention, taking it apart and rebuilding it a bunch of times until he can figure out how to make a version that can be used by baselines. That converts it from q-tech to Nova tech. Then he repeats the same process with the novatek a bunch of times until he comes up with a model that baselines can make themselves. That produces core-tech.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 01-11-2022, 05:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dat